{"name":"Leek Blossom Pink","hex":"#bca3b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vegetable of variety Allium ampeloprasum, having edible leaves and an onion-like bulb but with a milder flavour than the onion.","Any of several species of Allium, broadly resembling the domesticated plant in appearance in the wild."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leek"},{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leek","blocks":[{"text":"A leek is a biennial vegetable, a cultivar of Allium ampeloprasum, the broadleaf wild leek. The edible part of the plant is a bundle of leaf sheaths that is sometimes colloquially called a \"stem\" or \"stalk\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg/330px-Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leek","wikidata":"Q1807269"},{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom","wikidata":"Q2047589"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/500px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/1280px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/500px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh leeks sautéing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/500px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/1280px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/500px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.